    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d775">

                <pb facs="0788" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg676"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conference 184.01502/27:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-12"><hi rendition="#italic">May 12,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received in Paris, 9:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>366. Following from Greene, Libau.</p>
                <p>“Greene, 31, May 11: Actual distribution
                    American food begun under Major Brookings in Libau, May 9, through Municipal
                    Council. <pb facs="0789" n="677" xml:id="pg677"/> Flour also <hi
                        rendition="#italic">en route</hi> Windau and shortly to Mitau and Tuckum.
                    All distribution through Municipal Councils as no national government. As
                    privation exists mainly in cities this relieves situation.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p rendition="#right">Greene”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
